    "voltage": 24,
    "note": "Electric winches and sail-handling furlers, electrical side only. Primary (Harken 60.2 STEA 24H, sheet 350) and Main (sheet 351) winches each have a port+stbd unit: Harken DSS (Digital Safe Switch) decoder -> contactor (DFR70/DFR60 24HR control box) -> 24V winch motor; the +/- DC feed (W350/W351/W352/W353 from sheet 400) lands on the shared PRI_WIN_*/MAIN_WIN_* nodes (DCMS_F07-F10, 80A each). A common 5A control fuse -F23 (WINCHES/FURLER CTRL) on +MSB feeds the winch/furler control logic (-RCS rotary/current-sensor, -K30 WINCHES CONTROL relay) shared with the furlers; E-STOP relay -K01 (sheet 300) provides interlock contacts. Mooring winch (Maxwell RVC2500, sheet 360): solenoid box -A1 driven by Harken BRS102/P up/down buttons -S1/-S2, fed from shared MOORING_WINCH (DCMS_F11). Jib furler (Furlex 400 TDE, sheet 361): 900W motor -M1 via furler connection box, IN/OUT control, two Harken DSS decoders, fed from shared JIB_FURLER (DCMS_F12). Boom furler (Reckmann BFE 125, sheets 366/371): JB370 contactor -K370 / Bluesea 9012 + control box, Reckmann drive motor, pedestal buttons UNFURL/FLATTEN/FURL/BRAKE (-S04/-S05/-S09) at +PED_SB, fed FURLBOOM+/- from sheet 400. Mast furler (RC 24V F324, sheet 368): control box, Harken DSS, drive motor -M2, IN/OUT, fed FURL_MAST+/- from sheet 400. Transom door winch (sheet 370/371): Linak LA33 pusher actuator -M1 (door pusher) and DC winch motor -M2, reversing contactor -K_HYD (T6415-24 150A) + current-limitation card, time/sequence relays K1-K4, UP/DOWN buttons -S7/-S8, door-closed sensor -B01, fed +24VDC via F24 on MSB; radio remote Quick RRC -A1 + key switch -S01 on sheets 372/373. Table lift (Danaher TC16-24T, sheet 380): motor -M_LIFT1 via 1-0-2 keylock selector -S01/-S1, fed LIFT TABLE+/- from sheet 465. Hydraulic pump (sheet 390/391): HYD motor -M2 + solenoid -K391 (Bluesea 9012), SAIL HYDR switch -S01, fed HYDRAULICS+/- from sheet 400. NOTE: 350/351/360/361/390 are titled HYDRAULIC SYSTEM - the powered sail-handling/winch drive is hydraulic; the modelled DC side is the control/solenoid/decoder electrical circuit plus the electric winch motors."
  },
